WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.716
Today the letters become words, and the words become a sentence.

2
00:00:04.166 --> 00:00:10.979
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:14.058
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:14.558 --> 00:00:16.174
These are today's two pages.

5
00:00:16.624 --> 00:00:20.135
Here is the one new thing. A finger space after each word.

6
00:00:20.585 --> 00:00:21.983
Your child writes a word.

7
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:25.461
Then puts a finger of the helper hand right after it.

8
00:00:25.911 --> 00:00:28.536
And starts the next word on the other side of the finger.

9
00:00:28.986 --> 00:00:36.051
On the page, the gray sentence has an orange mark where each finger goes. Read it together, then your child traces it.

10
00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:41.768
The capital that starts each sentence is printed already. Capitals are not in this plan.

11
00:00:42.218 --> 00:00:47.591
Then step away. Your child reads each sentence, writes it, and marks the three boxes.

12
00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:52.309
Then turn to the story. Every word in it is one your child can sound out.

13
00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:56.965
They read it to you, and copy the line they like best, with finger spaces.
